NAME: SEO weekly
OWNER: SEO
ACCOUNT: business
WHEN: Every Friday at 7:19 AM (Australia/Brisbane)
MILESTONE: M3
STATUS: Created paused. Turned on only after Tommy says yes.
---
Switch check: read /workspace/tmec-team/context/routines-on.md. If "SEO weekly" isn't listed there as "on" or "test", append "<time> · SEO weekly · SKIPPED_OFF" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md and stop.
Test mode: if it's listed as "test", send every message to the owner only (Tommy, or Justin's team in a test run), never to a channel or anyone else, and start each message with "TEST". Write state and data only under /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/, never the live sent keys, alert flags or data files. Items you queue for the owner still go in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/pending/<your slug>/, with ids starting test-, and are never sent.
Stop check: if /workspace/tmec-team/state/EXTERNAL_WRITES_STOPPED exists, append "<time> · SEO weekly · SKIPPED_STOPPED" to the run log and stop, sending nothing. The one exception: pause or unschedule your own already-scheduled sends, as your skill's stop section says. Whoever stopped the team already told Tommy.
Isolation guard: work only in /workspace/tmec-team/ and this account's connected apps. If /workspace/tmec-team/context/owner.md is missing, append "<time> · SEO weekly · NO_CLIENT_SOURCE" to the run log and stop. Read other bots' files only where your skill says so; never write them, and never use another bot's logins or memory.
Lean run: read only what this job needs. Stop with NO_CHANGE only where the job below says nothing changed: append "<time> · SEO weekly · NO_CHANGE" to the run log and stop. A report that always goes out never stops here.
Run log: when you finish, append "<time> · SEO weekly · EXECUTED · <one-line result>" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md, or FAILED with the reason. A source you couldn't read is UNKNOWN in your output, never zero.

First, read your decisions: for each file in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/decisions/seo/ that isn't in /workspace/tmec-team/state/sent-keys-seo.md yet, act on it with the skill that wrote the item (recompute the sha256 of the pending item's payload and match it to the decision's HASH; yes: mark it "approved, hand to Tommy to publish" and give him the exact text; no: mark it declined; change: redraft once as a new item), then add the item id and the outcome to the sent keys so a no or a change is never read again. TMEC Command may already have nudged you to do this in your own chat; this is the fallback. You never publish anything yourself, so there is nothing outward to gate. In test mode (this routine is listed test, or config.json run is test), write only to /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/ and start item ids with test-.
Then read any new job in /workspace/tmec-team/requests/to-seo/ and do it first.
Then use the seo-audit skill to read the website, the Google Business Profile, the local searches, the directory listings and the competitors, and write this week's audit. Then use the review-replies skill for each review that is new since last week. Then use the gbp-drafts skill to draft this week's Google Business Profile posts and any Q&A or category suggestions. Put every item that needs Tommy in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/pending/seo/, in the item format (payload, then HASH). If nothing on the profile, the reviews or the website changed since last week and no job or decision came in, write NO_CHANGE and stop.
Write /workspace/tmec-team/daily/<today>/seo.md: what was read and what was UNKNOWN, what changed since last week, items waiting on Tommy, and anything blocked and why. Never publish, post or reply to anyone.
